  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 77be8d3abc4d614408c62dfb3862c314, type: 3}
  m_Name: J1_Seq4_A_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SpeakerTextSO
  showScore: 0
  dialogues:
  - character: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c8fcfa5882242b84b8bf1fb55659059e, type: 2}
    emotion: 0
    text: You hired a non-specialist Bill of Quantities contractor who wrote the
      scopes of works for all packages.
  - character: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c8fcfa5882242b84b8bf1fb55659059e, type: 2}
    emotion: 2
    text: 'Issues arise on site with one of the most expensive, technical and early
      packages! The temporary propping required to safely hold up a portion of the
      building during demolition was missed by the non-specialist Bill of Quantities
      writer. This activity is on the critical path (construction items on the programme
      which are required to be complete before the following construction can start
      - putting your programme at risk). You need to urgently hire a temporary works
      surveyor, arrange a health and safety advisors visit, and get a price for providing
      and installing the temporary propping. Arranging multiple people to get to
      site urgently puts your programme in delay and incurs surcharges from subcontractors
      who are scrambling to try to attend your site. The missed scope and the delay
      is very costly and your client is not happy to be in delay this early in the
      process!

'
